cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the paper below."
title: "PFM-LS: A Level Set Method on Particle Flow Maps, in NVIDIA Warp"
type: software
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/jinjinhe2001/Particle-Flowmap-Levelset"
abstract: >-
  A GPU implementation in NVIDIA Warp of the level set method on particle flow maps (PFM-LS), with 2D and 3D level
  sets, the paper's interface-tracking benchmarks (Zalesak's disk, LeVeque's vortex, the Distorted flow and the 3D
  deformed sphere), the paper's 2D droplet-splash free-surface example and a 2D dam break.
keywords:
  - level set method
  - particle flow map
  - interface tracking
  - free-surface flow
  - NVIDIA Warp
  - GPU
